# Sayso engine @VERSION@

This is the speech engine of Sayso for @SYSTEM@. It turns audio into text. Sayso starts it as a separate program and talks to it with a protocol. Your own program can do the same.

The engine has the version of the Sayso release that it comes with.

## Requirements

@REQUIREMENTS@

## Run the engine

Set `SAYSO_MODELS_DIR` to a folder for the model files. The engine makes the folder when it is not there. Do not let two engines use the same folder at the same time.

```
@RUN@
```

The engine reads requests from stdin and writes replies and events to stdout. Each message is one line of JSON (NDJSON). The engine stops when stdin closes.

To check that the engine works, send a `hello` request. The reply has the version of the engine, the version of the protocol, and the features of the engine. The engine stops when stdin closes, so keep stdin open for a moment, as this command does.

```
@HELLO@
```

## Protocol and conformance suite

The protocol is described in [docs/engine-protocol.md](https://github.com/watzon/sayso/blob/v@VERSION@/docs/engine-protocol.md). The text of the protocol has the MIT license.

The conformance suite checks that an engine follows the protocol. It is the crate `sayso-engine-conformance` in the [Sayso repository](https://github.com/watzon/sayso/tree/v@VERSION@/crates/sayso-engine-conformance). To run the checks that need no model, use Rust and run this command in a copy of the repository:

```
cargo run -p sayso-engine-conformance -- <path to the engine>
```

## Licenses

The engine has the GPL-3.0-only license. The text is in `LICENSE`. The licenses of the third-party code in the engine are in the folder `licenses`.
